# Starforge Skill Tree (54 nodes). Nodes never grant combat bonuses at the start of a run.
# Instead they buy starting hull/shields, ships, economy perks, "DRAFT CARD" nodes that add a
# new upgrade (main.RUN_UPGRADE_POOL id in "unlocks_upgrade") to the level-up draft pool, and
# "EVOLVE" nodes that upgrade a sub weapon once it's drafted ("evolves", 3 marks each).
# The tree is laid out in rings around the (0, 0) core: a node's ring is its depth (get_ring),
# "pos" puts it on that ring (radius RING_R0 + RING_STEP * ring) inside its wing's sector.
# Rogue Legacy style, a node only shows once its parent is owned and its ring is open, and rings
# open as the player's Knowledge (ranks bought) grows (MetaSave.get_knowledge_level).
# The hangar camera follows the selection.
